1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,220
What does 'a cold welcome' refer to?
“冷遇”指的是什么？

2
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:18,210
What does 'a cold welcome' refer to?
“冷遇”指的是什么？

3
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:24,270
On Wednesday evening, we went to the Town Hall.
星期三的晚上，我们去了市政厅。

4
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:32,710
It was the last day of the year and a large crowd of people had gathered under the Town Hall clock.
那是一年的最后一天，一大群人聚集在市政厅的大钟下面。

5
00:00:34,250 --> 00:00:38,040
It would strike twelve in twenty minutes' time.
再过20分钟，大钟将敲响12下。

6
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:46,060
Fifteen minutes passed and then, at five to twelve, the clock stopped.
15分钟过去了，就在11点55分时，大钟停了。

7
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:51,510
The big minute hand did not move.
那根巨大的分针不动了。

8
00:00:52,230 --> 00:00:56,510
We waited and waited, but nothing happened.
我们等啊等啊，可情况没有变化。

9
00:00:57,540 --> 00:00:59,690
Suddenly someone shouted.
突然有人喊道：

10
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:06,610
'It's two minutes past twelve! The clock has stopped!'
“已经12点零2分了！那钟已经停了！”

11
00:01:08,510 --> 00:01:10,120
I looked at my watch.
我看了一下我的手表。

12
00:01:10,230 --> 00:01:11,220
It was true.
果真如此。

13
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:15,810
The big clock refused to welcome the New Year.
那座大钟不愿意迎接新年。

14
00:01:16,740 --> 00:01:22,070
At that moment, everybody began to laugh and sing.
此时，大家已经笑了起来，同时唱起了歌。
